  "summary": "Reported: CEO Dana Whitfield (VIP, Executive, America/New_York, usual hours 08:00-18:00) got a new iPhone yesterday; Duo pushes no longer arrive; needs VPN for a board prep call at 2 PM today. Checked: account active, sign_in_blocked false, vpn_access true, failed_login_count 0. Duo enrolled (duo_push) on the old phone, enrolled_at 2025-12-15, so the enrollment still points at the old device. Sign-in logs for the last 14 days show 10 successful sign-ins (VPN from residential 198.51.100.21, M365 from corporate 203.0.113.10), all during usual hours, all Duo push, zero failed_password, zero mfa_denied, no hosting networks, New York only. No red flags of compromise. Laptop BL-LT-0101 online, last check-in 2026-10-11, no warnings. Needed: per KB-004 new-phone path, verify identity by callback to the number on file, then re-activate Duo Mobile on the new iPhone and send a test push. Tier 1 cannot do the Duo re-activation or the callback verification from these tools. Note: the triage record said user_blocked true, but lookup_user shows sign_in_blocked false; I did not request a block and no block is needed based on the logs. Time-sensitive: VPN needed by 2 PM.",
  "reason": "Duo re-activation for a replaced phone (KB-004) requires callback identity verification and a technician to re-enroll Duo Mobile; Tier 1 tools cannot complete it. Account is a VIP executive with a 2 PM deadline."
